data: {"type":"message","content":{"type":"ai","content":"No, 221 is not a prime number because it can be factored into 13 × 17.","tool_calls":[],"tool_call_id":null,"run_id":"01a1ea2b-21fd-7453-a102-7281a64b51b6","agent":null,"reasoning":"The user is asking whether 221 is a prime number. Let me think about this mathematically.\n\nA prime number is a number greater than 1 that has no positive divisors other than 1 and itself.\n\nTo check if 221 is prime, I need to see if it has any divisors other than 1 and 221.\n\nLet me check some common factors:\n- 221 is not divisible by 2 (it's odd)\n- 2+2+1 = 5, not divisible by 3\n- Doesn't end in 0 or 5, so not divisible by 5\n- Let me check 7: 221 ÷ 7 = 31.57... (not divisible)\n- Let me check 11: 221 ÷ 11 = 20.09... (not divisible)\n- Let me check 13: 221 ÷ 13 = 17\n\nSo 221 = 13 × 17, which means it has divisors other than 1 and itself. Therefore, 221 is NOT a prime number.\n\nI need to answer in one sentence as requested.","truncated":false,"response_metadata":{"finish_reason":"stop","model_name":"qwen3.5:9b","system_fingerprint":"fp_ollama","model_provider":"openai"},"custom_data":{}}}

